  "$comment": "CANONICAL QUESTION CATALOGUE — the fixed clinical questions, shared by the Java and Python planners. The medical content of every question is frozen here; an LLM may later rephrase for readability but can never invent a question, change what one asks, or add an option. Business logic keys off optionCode/questionId, never display text. Two runtimes with two hand-written catalogues would eventually ask different questions of the same patient, so there is exactly one.",
